    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: The loan was approved on 19 June 2020, signed on 2 July 2020, and became effective on 13 August 2020. Implementation was satisfactorily carried out. Social assistance top-ups have been provided through the food stamp program (e-cards and vouchers for adults and children), and through the child money program (direct transfers to children&apos;s bank accounts). As discussed and recorded in the MOU of the loan fact-finding mission of the Second Shock-Responsive Social Protection Project in November 2020, ADB has approved a minor change in implementation arrangement to add a new category for Project Management Support and Administration under this project, with reallocation of loan proceeds. The loan closed in April 2021. ADB Controllers to reflect financial closure in LFIS.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: FSP monthly benefit level increased to MNT32,000 per adult and MNT16,000 per child for 5 months May to September 2020.Actual data to be included in the PCR.CMP monthly benefit level increased to MNT100,000 per child for 6 months April to September 2020 and later extended for a further 3 months October to December 2020 (ADB financing covered 5 months, no claim for July 2020).</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
